 {
  "verse_id": "tsa-a21-v03",
  "song": "tsa-a21",
  "verse": 3,
  "lines": [
   "Therein — the universe made of mere consciousness,",
   "and consciousness of vimarśa-nature, and vimarśa's",
   "sound-nature established: of the world-thing",
   "and its manifold act-fruit connections,",
   "whatever contemplation that is — that is scripture.",
   "Whole scripture, in fact, is one-fruit-attaining",
   "by one-duty-declaration alone; but there,",
   "by the Lord's necessity-power-glory,",
   "people's establishment stands part by part."
  ],
  "sanskrit_cite": "tatra saṃvinmātramaye viśvasmin saṃvidi ca vimarśātmikāyāṃ vimarśasya ca śabdanātmakatāyāṃ siddhāyāṃ sakalajaganniṣṭhavastunaḥ tadgatasya ca karmaphalasambandhavaicitryasya yat vimarśanaṃ tad eva śāstram iti parameśvarasvabhāvābhinna eva samastaḥ śāstrasaṃdarbho vastuta ekaphalaprāpakaḥ ekādhikāryuddeśenaiva tatra tu parameśvaraniyatiśaktimahimnaiva bhāge bhāge rūḍhiḥ lokānām iti",
