 {
  "verse_id": "tsa-a21-v04",
  "song": "tsa-a21",
  "verse": 4,
  "lines": [
   "Some sit rūḍhi in Veda-tradition-and-rest,",
   "in the Māyā-difference-contemplation self;",
   "others just that kind by liberation-claim,",
   "in Sāṃkhya-Vaiṣṇava-scriptures-and-rest;",
   "others in separated-Śiva-nature's reflected essence,",
   "in Śaiva-Siddhānta-and-rest; others",
   "in all-pervasive Lordhood's reflected essence,",
   "in Maṅgala-and-rest; but some very rare",
   "in the Trika order's self — the Lord's own nature,",
   "reflected, bound by exhaustive-limitation-free-bliss",
   "supreme-truth-made-of-consciousness;",
   "but some by earlier-abandonment order",
   "or by transcendence — thus one-fruit-attainment",
   "from one āgama alone."
  ],
  "sanskrit_cite": "kecit māyocitabhedaparāmarśātmani vedāgamādiśāstre rūḍhāḥ anye tathāvidha eva mokṣābhimānena sāṃkhyavaiṣṇavaśāstrādau pare tu viviktaśivasvabhāvāmarśanasāre śaivasiddhāntādau anye sarvamayaparameśvaratāmarśanasāre mataṃgādiśāstre kecit tu viralaviralāḥ samastāvacchedavandhyasvātantryānandaparamārthasaṃvinmayaparameśvarasvarūpāmarśanātmani śrītrikaśāstrakrame kecit tu pūrvapūrvatyāgakrameṇa laṅghanena vā ity evam ekaphalasiddhiḥ ekasmād eva āgamāt",
